---
interface Props { kind: 'locks' | 'rules' | 'index'; number: number; }
const { kind, number } = Astro.props;
const configs = {
 locks: {
  title:'A waiting change can hold up a later reader',
  note:'Illustrative lock ordering on products. Time runs through the steps, with no duration scale. The timeout branch gives up the change attempt while the earlier reader stays open.',
  labels:['Earlier reader A','Schema change B','Later reader C'],
  options:['Change times out','Earlier reader commits'],
  states:[
   {boxes:[['ACCESS SHARE held','SELECT finished; transaction open','held'],['Not started','Needs ACCESS EXCLUSIVE','idle'],['Not started','Needs ACCESS SHARE','idle']],line:'A has finished its SELECT, but keeps the table lock until its transaction ends.',ex:'A reads products inside an explicit transaction. Finishing the SELECT does not release its ACCESS SHARE table lock.'},
   {boxes:[['ACCESS SHARE held','Transaction still open','held'],['ACCESS EXCLUSIVE waiting','Blocked by A','wait'],['Not started','Needs ACCESS SHARE','idle']],line:'B → waits for → A',ex:'B requests the strong lock for ADD COLUMN. It cannot acquire it while A holds ACCESS SHARE. The column has not been added.'},
   {boxes:[['ACCESS SHARE held','Transaction still open','held'],['ACCESS EXCLUSIVE waiting','Blocked by A','wait'],['ACCESS SHARE waiting','Behind B’s conflicting request','wait']],line:'C → waits behind → B → waits for → A',ex:'C arrives after B. Its read lock would coexist with A’s, but it cannot pass the earlier conflicting strong-lock request. Waiting schema work now delays ordinary reads.'},
   {boxes:[['ACCESS SHARE held','Transaction still open','held'],['Lock timeout','Statement failed; ROLLBACK next','bad'],['SELECT completes','Sees the original schema','held']],line:'B leaves the queue → C can read alongside A',ex:'B reaches its lock timeout. Its request leaves the queue and C can read, even though A has not ended. Roll back B’s failed explicit transaction before reusing it.'},
  ],
  alternate:{boxes:[['COMMIT','Releases ACCESS SHARE','idle'],['Lock acquired → change → COMMIT','Releases ACCESS EXCLUSIVE','held'],['SELECT completes','After B releases its strong lock','held']],line:'A ends → B changes and commits → C can read',ex:'A commits before the limit. B acquires its strong lock, adds the column and commits promptly. C can proceed only after B releases it; doing other work inside B’s transaction would extend the blockage.'}
 },
 rules:{
  title:'Non-null does not mean correctly converted',
  note:'A separate diagnostic P7 state: price 22.00, stale hundredths 2000. P3 and P9 are already 4.50/450 and 35.00/3500. The columns show enforcement and proof separately; the range rule is omitted here.',
  labels:['Committed P7','Rules on new writes','Existing population proved'],
  states:[
   {boxes:[['22.00 / 2000','Missing: 0 · Different: 1','bad'],['No new rule','A stale pair can be written','idle'],['No proof','Job completion is insufficient','idle']],line:'0 missing values ≠ agreement',ex:'Every new value is present, yet P7 is wrong. The unequal-value count exposes what the null count misses.'},
   {boxes:[['22.00 / 2000','The old violation remains','bad'],['NOT VALID rules installed','Reject new missing or unequal pairs','held'],['Not yet validated','Old rows were not scanned','wait']],line:'New writes: enforced ✓     Existing rows: unchecked',ex:'Install enforced NOT VALID not-null and agreement constraints, then commit. They check subsequent inserted or updated rows without certifying the old population.'},
   {boxes:[['22.00 / 2000','Still stale','bad'],['Both rules enforced','An unrelated update can also fail','held'],['NOT NULL: valid','Agreement: validation fails','bad']],line:'A successful not-null validation still leaves the conversion unproved',ex:'Not-null validation succeeds. Agreement validation finds the stale 2000 and fails. The installed agreement rule remains enforced on new writes.'},
   {boxes:[['22.00 / 2200','Repair from the current price','held'],['Both rules enforced','Bridge writers preserve the pair','held'],['Agreement: still not valid','Repair did not run validation','wait']],line:'Repair values → run validation again',ex:'A guarded current-row update repairs P7 to 2200. Correct data and a recorded validation are distinct states.'},
   {boxes:[['22.00 / 2200','Missing: 0 · Different: 0','held'],['Both rules enforced','Later writes must satisfy them','held'],['Both valid','Existing rows now checked','held']],line:'Enforcement + completed validation = an established rule',ex:'Agreement validation now succeeds. Existing rows satisfy the relation and the enforced rules preserve it for subsequent writes. Caller acceptance remains a separate deployment decision.'},
  ]
 },
 index:{
  title:'An index can exist before a query may use it',
  note:'Conceptual CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY on the customer-history key. Boxes describe successive committed states, not elapsed time or a complete list of internal phases.',
  labels:['Index definition','Writes maintain it','Queries may use it'],
  states:[
   {boxes:[['orders_history exists','indislive = true','held'],['Not ready','indisready = false','idle'],['Not valid','indisvalid = false','idle']],line:'Catalogue entry ≠ usable access path',ex:'The concurrent build first records an invalid index. Finding its name proves only that a definition exists.'},
   {boxes:[['First build completed','More work remains','held'],['Ready for new tuples','indisready = true','held'],['Still invalid','indisvalid = false','wait']],line:'Foreground changes maintain the index while validation catches up',ex:'After the first build commits, writes maintain the new index. A second scan reconciles tuples missed while the first scan ran. Readiness for writes does not certify query completeness.'},
   {boxes:[['Validation scan completed','Old snapshots can remain','held'],['Ready','indisready = true','held'],['Still waiting','indisvalid = false','wait']],line:'End of a scan ≠ end of the command',ex:'The build can wait for older snapshots after its validation scan. A scan counter at its total cannot predict when those transactions will end.'},
   {boxes:[['Build completed','Check the exact definition','held'],['Ready','indisready = true','held'],['Valid','indisvalid = true','held']],line:'Validate the index → test representative query results and work',ex:'The command finishes with a valid index. Very old transactions can still limit immediate usability; use fresh representative sessions to check the intended query and retain the previous route until acceptance.'},
  ]
 }
};
const config=configs[kind];
---
<figure class="pg-scene" data-pg-scene data-config={JSON.stringify(config)} aria-label={config.title}>
 <div class="scene-title"><span>Figure {number}</span><p>{config.title}</p></div>
 {config.options && <div class="scene-options" role="group" aria-label="How the lock queue ends">{config.options.map((x,i)=><button type="button" data-choice={i} aria-pressed={i===0?'true':'false'}>{x}</button>)}</div>}
 <div class="scene-board">
  {config.labels.map((label,i)=><div class="scene-lane"><p class="lane-name">{label}</p><div data-box class={`state-box ${config.states[0].boxes[i][2]}`}><strong data-live data-state>{config.states[0].boxes[i][0]}</strong><span data-live data-detail>{config.states[0].boxes[i][1]}</span></div></div>)}
 </div>
 <p class="scene-link" data-live data-line>{config.states[0].line}</p>
 <p class="scene-explanation" data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite">{config.states[0].ex}</p>
 <div class="scene-controls" role="group" aria-label={`Figure ${number} playback`}><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / {config.states.length}</span></div>
 <div class="scene-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 <figcaption>{config.note}</figcaption>
 <details><summary>All stages, as text</summary><ol>{config.states.map(s=><li>{s.ex}</li>)}{config.alternate&&<li>{config.alternate.ex}</li>}</ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-pg-scene]')){
 const config=JSON.parse(root.dataset.config!);let choice=0;
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>config.states.length,draw:(i:number)=>{
  const state=choice===1&&i===config.states.length-1?config.alternate:config.states[i];
  root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-box]').forEach((box,j)=>{box.className='state-box '+state.boxes[j][2];box.querySelector('[data-state]')!.textContent=state.boxes[j][0];box.querySelector('[data-detail]')!.textContent=state.boxes[j][1];});
  root.querySelector('[data-line]')!.textContent=state.line;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=state.ex;
 }});
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-choice]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{choice=Number(button.dataset.choice);root.querySelectorAll('[data-choice]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));player.render();}));
}
</script>
<style is:global>
.pg-scene {margin:2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);font: .86rem/1.55 var(--font-sans);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;}
.pg-scene .scene-title{padding:1rem 1rem .2rem;}.pg-scene .scene-title>span{color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;}.pg-scene .scene-title p{font:600 1rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);margin:.3rem 0;}
.pg-scene .scene-board{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.7rem;padding:1rem;}.pg-scene .lane-name{font:.75rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary);min-height:2em;margin:0 0 .5rem;}
.pg-scene .state-box{padding:.8rem .65rem;min-height:8rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.55rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface);border-radius:3px;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}.pg-scene .state-box strong{font-size:.87rem;}.pg-scene .state-box span{font-size:.76rem;}.pg-scene .held{border-color:var(--teal);border-top-width:4px;}.pg-scene .wait{border-color:var(--gold);border-style:dashed;border-top-width:4px;}.pg-scene .bad{border-color:var(--coral);border-top-width:4px;}.pg-scene .idle{border-top-width:4px;}
.pg-scene .scene-link{margin:0 1rem 1rem;font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-mono);white-space:normal;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}.pg-scene .scene-explanation{margin:1rem;padding:.2rem 0 .2rem .8rem;border-left:3px solid var(--teal);font:.88rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);min-height:5em;}
.pg-scene .scene-controls,.pg-scene .scene-options{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.8rem 1rem;background:var(--color-surface);}.pg-scene button{font:.78rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface-alt);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:3px;padding:.4rem .6rem;cursor:pointer;}.pg-scene button[aria-pressed=true]{border-color:var(--teal);box-shadow:inset 0 -3px 0 var(--teal);}.pg-scene button[aria-disabled=true]{color:var(--color-text-secondary);border-style:dashed;}.pg-scene button:focus-visible,.pg-scene summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px;}.pg-scene [data-step]{margin-left:auto;font-size:.73rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);}.pg-scene .scene-hold{height:3px;background:var(--color-rule);}.pg-scene .scene-hold span{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:var(--teal);}.pg-scene figcaption{margin:0;padding:.8rem 1rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);}.pg-scene details{padding:.5rem 1rem 1rem;font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);}.pg-scene summary{cursor:pointer;}.pg-scene li{margin:.55rem 0;}
@media(max-width:550px){.pg-scene .scene-board{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.65rem;}.pg-scene .scene-lane{display:grid;grid-template-columns:6.3rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:.6rem;align-items:center;}.pg-scene .state-box{min-height:0;padding:.65rem;gap:.2rem;}.pg-scene .lane-name{min-height:0;margin:0;}.pg-scene .scene-explanation{min-height:0;}}
</style>
